From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MoneroOne <devs@monero.one>
Date: Mon, 5 May 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] HIDAPI_DUMMY trumps host hidapi during cross-compile

When cross-compiling for iOS, find_package(HIDAPI) may pick up the
host's homebrew-installed hidapi and set HIDAPI_FOUND/HAVE_HIDAPI.
Those headers live at /opt/homebrew/include/hidapi which is NOT on
the iOS sysroot include path, so when device_io_hid.hpp's
`#if defined(HAVE_HIDAPI)` block tries to pull in <hidapi/hidapi.h>
the iOS compile aborts with "fatal error: 'hidapi/hidapi.h' file
not found".

HIDAPI_DUMMY mode exists precisely so device_ledger / device_io_hid
can be compiled without a real hidapi present (the host app supplies
the byte-swap shim instead). Skip the host hidapi pickup entirely
when DUMMY is set so HAVE_HIDAPI never gets defined.
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -699,12 +699,17 @@ if (HIDAPI_DUMMY)
 endif()

 # Final setup for hid
-if (HIDAPI_FOUND)
+# HIDAPI_DUMMY trumps HIDAPI_FOUND — when cross-compiling for iOS,
+# find_package may pick up a host (homebrew) hidapi whose headers are
+# not on the iOS sysroot. Defining HAVE_HIDAPI in that state pulls
+# <hidapi/hidapi.h> into the iOS compile and fails. Skip the host
+# hidapi entirely when DUMMY is set.
+if (HIDAPI_FOUND AND NOT HIDAPI_DUMMY)
   message(STATUS "Using HIDAPI include dir at ${HIDAPI_INCLUDE_DIR}")
   add_definitions(-DHAVE_HIDAPI)
   include_directories(${HIDAPI_INCLUDE_DIR})
   link_directories(${LIBHIDAPI_LIBRARY_DIRS})
 else()
-  message(STATUS "Could not find HIDAPI")
+  message(STATUS "HIDAPI not used (DUMMY=${HIDAPI_DUMMY}, FOUND=${HIDAPI_FOUND})")
 endif()

 # Trezor support check
